; claude: the programming tools (CATALOG.md's section): TinyBasic, Tiny
; BASIC (1976) on a 1977 home computer's screen, over libs/languages/basic and
; the playground's Teletype way (plan_terminal.md, section 5); TinyVi
; and TinyEmacs, the two text editors, full-screen programs of the
; terminal over appkits/editor and the Textmode way (Emacs's Lisp is
; libs/languages/lisp); TinyTurboPascal, Turbo Pascal 7's IDE in text
; mode, over the same appkit and libs/languages/pascal's P-code. Laid
; out like office/: the programs here, software/ for the golden frames,
; web/ for the browser, tty/ for the editors in a real terminal.
;
; What else it might contain, each Tiny and after a famous original:
;  - a debugger (the Smalltalk-80 one): a running program's stack and
;    state, the inspector of plan_inspect_teaching.md;
;  - a notebook or REPL (Mathematica 1988, Jupyter): cells of code and
;    what they print, pictures included.
; Built on gui/ and the appkits (richtext, document).
(executables
  (names TinyBasic TinyVi TinyEmacs TinyTurboPascal)
  (modules TinyBasic TinyVi TinyEmacs TinyTurboPascal)
  (libraries
    basic ; Basic_parse, Basic_run, Basic_session
    appkit_editor ; Tui_vi, Tui_emacs, Tui_turbo
    elm_playground
    elm_playground_native ; implem of virtual elm_playground
  )
)
